# Crush OS

Teaching kernel in C. David drives design. Push back on low-value or out-of-scope work.

Read `AGENTS.md`, `docs/principles.md`, `docs/architecture.md`, and `docs/roadmap.md` before changing direction.

## Always

- Follow `CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md`. Explicit, plain language. No sarcasm as the default.
- Simplest honest solution. One lab, one idea.
- C modules, not class hierarchies. Docs ship with the work.
- Format C with `clang-format` only (LLVM, 4 spaces, 100 columns). Leave `*.S` alone.

## Refuse unless a new ADR or an explicit Phase 2 ask

- POSIX, `fork`/`exec` first, VFS, libc, Unix shell, ELF-as-done
- UEFI, long mode, x86_64 guest, Limine, GRUB, Multiboot
- Microkernel, SMP, networking, GUI
- A second formatter or hosted `clang-tidy`

## Example

```text
# Bad: "add GRUB so we can skip the boot sector"
# Good: keep our BIOS sector; add a second stage only if the kernel no longer fits
```
